eeks it's  ideal  but you know it's hard so you can cheat  it in 10 days and we have ways of making  the recovery much faster today that just  weren't available 10 years ago so i have  things that i can do  you know techniques and instruments and  and you know and lasers that help  recovery get rid of bruising you know  there are different uh treatments that  we do one of them is hyperbaric oxygen  treatments where you go into a  hyperbaric oxygen chamber every day and  increases the blood supply and the  oxygen content of the tissue so the  healing is much faster and i've learned  these things because a lot of my  patients  need to be back in front of cameras  really quickly i take care of a lot of  people who have public faces and as a  result i needed to figure out a way to  get them back to work quicker because  they don't have a lot of down time  between you know shooting you know  shooting television shows or other  things you know  what percentage of celebrities are  people who have tv appearances who are  you know in their 50s or 60s have had  work done do you think oh so pretty much  everybody who's post who's 50 and above  has had work done  so if somebody men too  yeah men kind of can cheat until about  late 50s early 60s so there's definitely  an unfair um you know unfair disparity  between men and women in terms of the  way they age  women generally speaking around 50 start  to age more rapidly and by 52-53 their  face really changes  that's because women go through  menopause on average at about 50 to 51  years of age and within two years of  that change  the facial tissues drop so unfortunately  there is a big change and a shut off  that happens for women that accelerates  their aging process so on average  most women will consider this if they  don't aren't more proactive about doing  it around 50 because they notice that  things just don't hold up nicely the way  they used to  men get to get a pass it's usually  around 60 that this stuff really starts  to come apart so i usually will treat  most men later 50s to early 60s and most  later 40s to early 50s  so that's when i kind of see it but if  you see a celebrity  who's in her early to mid 50s and she  looks youthful she's had surgery  it's nobody escapes this unfortunately  i've been doing this for 20 years and  i've done about 4 000 facelifts  nobody escapes this and it doesn't mean  that they look abnormal because with  good surgery people look natural like  themselves but youthful  but you can't be 53 years old and look  like you're 40 without surgery it  doesn't happen  okay so it's not all olive oil then  okay i don't want to comment on that but  it's not a oil  i guess i just did  olive oil it's not in recommends i mean  you know i i give these excuses to my  patients you know when they say well  what am i going to say when people tell  me how great i look i said well if you  look natural you won't say anything you  tell people you lost weight you've been  drinking green juice you know you've  been doing more meditation people  associate a youthful but natural  appearance with good health  so it's very easy to blame it on things  like olive oil your diet your  antioxidant drinks your your vitamins  you know a new skincare regimen because  if you look normal  nobody really gets it it's only when you  have the distortion  and the classic look that comes with you  know more antiquated  facelift surgery or plastic surgery that  it gets a big alarm  so i give people these excuses all the  time like yeah just tell people that you  did these three things you know or that  you had a little bit of botox or you had  someone that you know i intense pulse  like there would be treating your  dermatologist's office it totally throws  people off because they're not really  looking at surgery  they're looking at somebody who looks  good and healthy and youthful and they  want to know what your secret is but  they don't think it's surgery they think  it's lifestyle choices  okay so what are the what are the  downsides here  like is is this type of thing  super invasive is it dangerous and just  do you need to go under general  anesthetic no so we don't use your  anesthesia at least i don't a lot of  surgeons do but we do something called  twilight sedation which is where you get  a little iv they give you some medicine  that just makes you kind of sleep but  you're not paralyzed with the two of  your lungs breathing gas so it's not  something where it's like a heavy  anesthesia that's very risky um  obviously all surgery has risks so it's  not risk-free but the thing is is that  when you're with an experienced  practitioner your risk of having a  significant complication from surgery is  probably less than one percent and even  then those problems if you have one  can be managed and remedied
 

